  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solomon Islands Biosecurity Development Program (SIBDP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SIBDP is a bilateral technical capacity and capability development program delivered by DAFF to strengthen the Solomon Islands Biosecurity System through technical and operational support to the SI Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock (MAL), and Biosecurity Solomon Islands (BSI). The program supports the delivery of plant and animal health technical training, surveillance and diagnostics and outbreak response. The program also includes a strategy and governance component to strengthen the ogranisational and institutional capacity and sustainability of the biosecurity system.</narrative>
  </description>
